[KiCad-IOS port] Round 22 crash hunt #1/#2: the footprint chooser
no longer builds its desktop-OpenGL 3D preview canvas on iOS, and
the field-properties footprint button carries stage traces.

Diagnosis (hidden_files/round22-bug-ledger.md #1/#2, census in
round22-hunt-crash.md): on the Round 21 build, Sean tapped a
schematic symbol's field properties, then the FOOTPRINT field's
library button, and the app crashed. The handler
(DIALOG_FIELD_PROPERTIES::OnTextValueSelectButtonClick) creates
FOOTPRINT_CHOOSER_FRAME via Kiway().Player(); that frame's
constructor calls build3DCanvas() unconditionally, which
constructs an EDA_3D_CANVAS — a desktop-OpenGL wxGLCanvas with
an 8x-MSAA attribute list. It is the only raw GL canvas
construction on any chooser path: every GAL editor canvas on
this port is forced to Cairo at the SwitchBackend choke point
(patches 0035/0036), but this canvas bypasses that funnel.
wxQt's GL support cannot fail cleanly (wxGLContext reports
m_isOk=true unconditionally; SetCurrent calls
QOpenGLWidget::makeCurrent regardless), and iOS has no desktop
OpenGL (the build's GL shim maps the headers to OpenGLES/ES3),
so the canvas's context/paint machinery hard-faults — the
round-14 S1 mechanism. The other two suspects were cleared by
reading: KIWAY_PLAYER::ShowModal carries the 0049(2) detach
since Round 20 and serves the device-working symbol chooser,
and the MAIL_SYMBOL_NETLIST payload is built null-guarded and
parsed defensively in KiwayMailIn. Every other door into the
chooser (symbol properties grid, both fields tables, Exchange
Footprints, Assign Component Classes, Insert Footprint) shares
this one constructor, so one fix covers them all.

Fix (all under #ifdef KICAD_IOS_PORT, desktop builds
byte-unchanged):
- build3DCanvas(): on iOS, skip the EDA_3D_CANVAS construction
  (the board-adapter setup above it is plain data and still
  runs); m_preview3DCanvas stays null. The 2D preview is a GAL
  panel already on Cairo and is unaffected.
- Null-guard every remaining m_preview3DCanvas use: the
  constructor's initial Show, updatePanelsVisibility(),
  updateViews(), and the destructor's GL-teardown hack.
- Hide the 3D toggle button and the "Show 3D viewer in own
  window" checkbox in the constructor (3D is a named
  non-working feature on this port), and make on3DviewReq
  return early as belt and braces.
- Stage traces (the exact faulting instruction inside the
  Qt/GL stack cannot be read off source, and no device crash
  log was available this round): the dialog handler traces
  "round22-fpchooser-click" before Player(); build3DCanvas
  traces "round22-chooser-3d-skipped"; the frame constructor
  traces "round22-fpchooser-frame-ready" on completion. If a
  crash remains on the next device verdict, the last trace in
  the log names the stage.

Gate: hidden_files/round22_gate.py requires the UTF-32LE
literals "round22-fpchooser-click" (libeeschema_kiface),
"round22-chooser-3d-skipped" and "round22-fpchooser-frame-ready"
(libpcbnew_kiface) in the shipped binaries; the Round 21 IPA
must FAIL all three.

Modified files:
  eeschema/dialogs/dialog_field_properties.cpp
  pcbnew/footprint_chooser_frame.cpp

